msgid "When the clause with <0>kui</0> or <1>kuna</1> comes first, the comma comes after it: <2>Kui ma koju jõuan, helistan sulle.</2> A short comparison takes no comma: <3>suurem kui Tartu</3>, as in lesson {comparing}."
msgstr "When the clause with <0>kui</0> or <1>kuna</1> comes first, the comma comes after it: <2>Kui ma koju jõuan, helistan sulle.</2> A short comparison takes no comma: <3>suurem kui Tartu</3>, as in lesson {comparing}."

msgid "When the clause with <0>kui</0> or <1>kuna</1> comes first, the main clause usually starts with its verb: <2>Kui ma koju jõuan, helistan sulle.</2> With <3>siis</3>, the subject can come first again: <4>Kui ma koju jõuan, siis ma helistan sulle.</4>"
msgstr "When the clause with <0>kui</0> or <1>kuna</1> comes first, the main clause usually starts with its verb: <2>Kui ma koju jõuan, helistan sulle.</2> With <3>siis</3>, the subject can come first again: <4>Kui ma koju jõuan, siis ma helistan sulle.</4>"

